From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Add HMA-OSS, TEESimulator and BRENE to Onigiri settings

Each module gets a row under Patch settings, like Play Integrity Fix: its switch stores the
choice in persist.sys.onigiri.<id> for the next start, and its name opens the module's page with
an On/Off bar, Status, a Version row that asks root for an update, and HMA-OSS's app rules or
BRENE's options. RootModPreferenceController describes the properties it reads and writes.

