+# Rows for the built-in root modules HMA-OSS (hma), TEESimulator (tee) and BRENE (brene). The key
+# picks the row: onigiri_<id> is the module switch (its row on the Onigiri page and the On/Off bar
+# on its own page), onigiri_brene_<option> a BRENE option, onigiri_<id>_status, _version and _rules
+# the rest of the module's page.
+#
+# A switch only stores the choice in persist.sys.onigiri.<id>[.<option>]. init applies it at the
+# next start and records what it started with in sys.onigiri.<id>.enabled and
+# sys.onigiri.brene.<option>; until then the change reads "after restart" and offers a restart.
+# sys.onigiri.<id>.state is what runs now: active, off, anything else reads Unavailable.
+#
+# Version asks root for an update with sys.onigiri.<id>.update=requested. Root answers checking,
+# then updated (sys.onigiri.<id>.pending_version waits for the next start), up_to_date,
+# incompatible or error. The row re-reads it every second while the page shows, for up to 180 s.
